---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="How we make money"
  description="Predikt earns affiliate commissions when readers sign up to platforms through our links. Here is our full, plain-English disclosure."
  path="/how-we-make-money"
>
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
    <h1>How we make money</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: some of our links are affiliate links. If you sign up to a
      platform through one of them, we may earn a commission: at no extra cost to
      you.
    </p>

    <h2>The details</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is free to read. We fund the site through affiliate partnerships
      with the platforms we write about. When you click certain links and then
      create or fund an account, the platform may pay us a referral commission.
    </p>
    <p>
      This <strong>never changes the price you pay</strong>, and it doesn't unlock
      anything different for you versus going to the platform directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Does it affect what we recommend?</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to recommend what genuinely fits your situation: especially your
      country and experience level. If a platform isn't available to you, we'll say
      so even though it means we earn nothing from you. Our long-term value depends
      on you trusting us, so honest guidance is also good business.
    </p>

    <h2>How links are labelled</h2>
    <p>
      Affiliate links are marked near the link itself and carry the appropriate
      technical tags. This page is our standing disclosure, in line with guidance
      such as the US FTC's rules on endorsements.
    </p>

    <h2>How the commissions are structured</h2>
    <p>
      Platforms typically pay affiliates in one of three ways: a flat fee per
      qualified user (CPA), a share of the trading fees those users generate over
      time (RevShare), or a mix of both (hybrid). We mention this so you can see
      there's nothing hidden: it's a standard referral arrangement. If you're
      curious about the mechanics, we wrote a full explainer:
      <a href="/guides/affiliate-programs-explained">how prediction market affiliate programs work</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Not financial advice.</strong> Everything here is educational. Trading
      on prediction markets carries risk; only use money you can afford to lose, and
      follow the laws and age limits where you live.
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
